            "type": "text/html"
          }
        ]
      },
      "note": [
        "Protected areas refer here to national parks, nature reserves, nature conservation areas and Natura 2000 areas. \r\n \r\n The statistics show new protected nature in the form of completely new protected areas from 1998 and onwards, based on the original date of valid for each area. Expansions of areas formed before 1998 are not included. \r\n \r\n Overlapping areas have been deducted. \r\n \r\n Data for all years are revised annually, to include changes for areas with older dates of valid.",
        "Rounded values \r\n Areas are rounded to even 100s. Consequently, sub-quantities cannot be summed to a total.",
        "The source of data on nature types and forest land is the Swedish Environmental Protection Agency’s National Land Cover Database (NMD). Statistics for all years are recalculated annually based on the latest available version of NMD."
      ],
